{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "35733986",
      "title": "Error Handling with Custom Errors",
      "sourceHash": "04658ce19e8f5caf090850fbcc7937a89fef32964e2c5abb736348e250af9e78",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.52,
          "end": 5.13,
          "en": "Now let's move on to error handling because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.13,
          "end": 7.59,
          "en": "of course fetching the data could go wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.59,
          "end": 12.336,
          "en": "And previously when using this user fact based solution",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.336,
          "end": 15.06,
          "en": "we handled errors manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.06,
          "end": 18.24,
          "en": "Now we're not handling errors anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.24,
          "end": 19.803,
          "en": "So how can we handle them?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21,
          "end": 23.305,
          "en": "Well, for example here when we see that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.305,
          "end": 25.14,
          "en": "the response is not okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.14,
          "end": 29.4,
          "en": "if it has a 400 ish or 500 ish status code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.4,
          "end": 34.195,
          "en": "what we can do in that case is we can return a different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.195,
          "end": 38.76,
          "en": "response, for example, or just return an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.76,
          "end": 41.61,
          "en": "Doesn't have to be a response, as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.61,
          "end": 44.19,
          "en": "Where we could add is error key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.19,
          "end": 48.597,
          "en": "and a message like 'could not fetch events'.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.53,
          "end": 51.669,
          "en": "So now we return this data package instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.669,
          "end": 55.353,
          "en": "of the response returned by our API request here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.49,
          "end": 59.62,
          "en": "In our component code we could now simply check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.229,
          "end": 62.062,
          "en": "if data.isError.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.12,
          "end": 66.57,
          "en": "So if this error property which we set here exists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.57,
          "end": 70.28999999999999,
          "en": "and is truth, and if that's the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.28999999999999,
          "end": 73.08,
          "en": "we could return a paragraph where we",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.08,
          "end": 76.26,
          "en": "output data dot message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.26,
          "end": 78.753,
          "en": "So where we output that data message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.92,
          "end": 83.4,
          "en": "With that we still have a pretty lean component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.4,
          "end": 87.9,
          "en": "We only added this code here and we have the error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.9,
          "end": 91.02,
          "en": "generation and handling code in our loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.02,
          "end": 93.12299999999999,
          "en": "where it belongs, arguably.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.11,
          "end": 96.27000000000001,
          "en": "If I now deliberately break this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.27000000000001,
          "end": 99.9,
          "en": "by sending the request to a path that doesn't exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.9,
          "end": 103.08,
          "en": "on the back end, you will see that I get this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 103.08,
          "end": 104.37,
          "en": "error message here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.37,
          "end": 106.416,
          "en": "Again, styling is a bit off, but we could",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.416,
          "end": 108.093,
          "en": "of course change this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.35,
          "end": 112.35,
          "en": "So that's one way of handling errors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.35,
          "end": 115.17,
          "en": "simply returning data that indicates that we have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.17,
          "end": 118.11,
          "en": "an error and then using that data appropriately",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.11,
          "end": 119.193,
          "en": "in the component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.6,
          "end": 123.09,
          "en": "Now I'll comment this out though because that's not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.09,
          "end": 126.66,
          "en": "how I'll do it here, because there is an alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.66,
          "end": 129.9,
          "en": "As an alternative to returning this data here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.9,
          "end": 133.95,
          "en": "to the component, we could throw an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.95,
          "end": 136.71,
          "en": "For this we can construct a new error object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.71,
          "end": 138.462,
          "en": "with the built in error constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.462,
          "end": 142.98,
          "en": "or we throw any other kind of object as an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.98,
          "end": 144.78,
          "en": "And here we could then also, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.78,
          "end": 147.286,
          "en": "include a message and say, 'could not fetch events'.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.286,
          "end": 148.413,
          "en": "Like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.85,
          "end": 152.61,
          "en": "Now, when an error gets thrown in a loader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.61,
          "end": 154.5,
          "en": "something special happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.5,
          "end": 159.5,
          "en": "React router will simply render the closest error element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.14,
          "end": 163.23,
          "en": "And you might remember we covered error elements earlier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.23,
          "end": 166.17000000000002,
          "en": "in this section when we added an error element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.17000000000002,
          "end": 169.86,
          "en": "to the Root Route to have a fallback page that would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 169.86,
          "end": 173.43,
          "en": "displayed in case of 4 0 4 errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 173.43,
          "end": 176.883,
          "en": "So if we navigated to paths that aren't supported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 177.93,
          "end": 181.77,
          "en": "Well, turns out that error element is not just there to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 181.77,
          "end": 186.09,
          "en": "show a fallback page in case of invalid route paths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 186.09,
          "end": 189.39,
          "en": "That is one use case but not the only one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.39,
          "end": 192.48,
          "en": "Instead, the error element will be shown",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.48,
          "end": 195.84,
          "en": "to the screen whenever an error is generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.84,
          "end": 199.953,
          "en": "in any route related code, including loaders.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.85,
          "end": 204.34,
          "en": "So therefore what we can do is we can add an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.68,
          "end": 210.09,
          "en": "page again here with pages and create our error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.09,
          "end": 213.423,
          "en": "page component in there and export this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 216.57,
          "end": 218.43,
          "en": "And then here we can of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 218.43,
          "end": 221.94299999999998,
          "en": "output a message like 'an error occurred' for a start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 223.2,
          "end": 227.1,
          "en": "Now we can go back to App.js and add error element here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 227.1,
          "end": 232.1,
          "en": "on this Root route and render our error page like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 232.53,
          "end": 235.92000000000002,
          "en": "For that of course, error page must be imported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 235.92000000000002,
          "end": 239.583,
          "en": "Then it's added here with error element on that Root path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 241.05,
          "end": 242.52,
          "en": "With that, this page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 242.52,
          "end": 244.89,
          "en": "this error page, will be displayed whenever",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 244.89,
          "end": 247.65,
          "en": "we basically have any kind of error anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 247.65,
          "end": 251.88,
          "en": "in our routes because even though I'm throwing an error here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 251.88,
          "end": 254.1,
          "en": "in the loader of the events page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 254.1,
          "end": 258.27,
          "en": "So in this route here, which is a deeply nested route,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 258.27,
          "end": 260.76,
          "en": "errors will bubble up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 260.76,
          "end": 264.36,
          "en": "We could add error element to this route as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 264.36,
          "end": 267.57,
          "en": "And in that case, this error element would be rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 267.57,
          "end": 270.48,
          "en": "if this loader threw an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 270.48,
          "end": 274.23,
          "en": "But we can also just have this Root level error element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 274.23,
          "end": 277.563,
          "en": "and the error would bubble up until it reaches that route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 278.73,
          "end": 280.38,
          "en": "So with that, if we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 280.38,
          "end": 282.36,
          "en": "you see that we get an error occurred",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 282.36,
          "end": 285.75,
          "en": "once we visit slash events and we get the same page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 285.75,
          "end": 288.99,
          "en": "if we try to visit an invalid route, by the way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 288.99,
          "end": 291.03,
          "en": "Of course the other routes still work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 291.03,
          "end": 293.943,
          "en": "but trying to visit events gives us this error.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}